cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "pinn: A Modular PyTorch Framework for Physics-Informed Neural Networks"
abstract: >-
  pinn is a modular PyTorch framework for solving forward and inverse partial
  differential equation problems with Physics-Informed Neural Networks, in which
  the governing equations are embedded directly in the training loss via
  automatic differentiation. It provides continuous-time and discrete-time
  Runge-Kutta solvers, a range of network architectures (Fourier-feature,
  multi-scale, attention, Bayesian, ensemble), adaptive loss weighting and
  sampling strategies, uncertainty quantification, transfer learning, distributed
  training, and model-serving utilities.
